  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-12 End
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I arrived at Hong Kong, where I met Jose Maria Basa who had constituted
      himself the special guardian of the Filipino students in that city. I was amused
      to see the methods of education with a spirit of patriotism developed thereby.
      I watched Chinese theater, as I had an interest in it. I learned a good amount
      on how they portrayed different actions, emotions, and stories. I met the exile
      and I was sympathetic with his struggles, and admired how he handled his struggles.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I then sailed for Japan, which I was surprised to be invited by the
      Spanish consulate. I graciously accepted the offer and was treated with hospitable
      courtesy. I was then offered a position, as a sort of interpreter, if I were
      to remain in the country. However, I refused. Afterwards, I made a considerable
      investigation of the various Japanese classes and acquired such facilities
      in the use of the language.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: A month or so had passed, when it was time for me to sail for San Francisco.
      I accompanied a Japanese newspaper man on the entire journey to London and
      acted as his interpreter.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I arrived at San Francisco, then started my journey to the Rocky Mountains,
      until I reached Chicago. I was surprised by the amount of cigar stores they
      had in San Francisco. I then made my way to Niagara Falls, then Albany, then
      to New York. After that, I made my way to England, I then lived with the exile
      named Doctor Antonio Maria Regidor.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "I then boarded with Mr. Beckett, organist of St. Paul\u2019s Church,
      at 37 Charlecote Crescent, in the favorite North West residence section. During
      my voyage, my interest in sleight-of-hand tricks was still there. The simple
      country folk, who we were looking on, thought I was performing miracles. In
      London, I received a gift from Mrs. Beckett, \"The Life and Adventures of Valentine
      Vox the Ventriloquist,\" showing that I amused her friends."
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
